OL,3,GNEWSADonating kidney to daughter a
OL,4,A'no-brainer', says dad
OL,5,
OL,6,FFather-of-two Brad Walker said it was a
OL,7,F"no-brainer" when he found out he could
OL,8,Fdonate his kidney to his five-year-old
OL,9,Fdaughter.
OL,11,FThe 28-year-old, from Chellaston,
OL,12,FDerby, said he "got lucky" to be a
OL,13,Ftransplant match for his daughter
OL,14,FNoa-Rae, who has nephrotic syndrome, a
OL,15,Fcondition which causes the kidneys to
OL,16,Fleak large amounts of protein into the
OL,17,Furine.
OL,19,FShe was diagnosed at the age of two
OL,20,Fbefore having both kidneys removed a
OL,21,Fyear later and has frequently missed
OL,22,Fschool because of illness.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
